# Infrastructure and Security Rules

- Inspect existing infrastructure and cost implications before editing.
- Run formatting and validation checks available in the repository.
- Review Terraform plans before applying. Never apply or destroy without explicit approval.
- Do not put credentials in source files, image layers, Terraform outputs, or logs.
- Prefer least-privilege IAM, GitHub OIDC, non-root containers, health probes, resource limits, and private networking where appropriate.
- Do not expose internal services publicly without a requirement.
- Warn about resources that may incur ongoing charges and explain teardown implications.
